Package: FSNA
Type: Package
Title: Fuzzy Social Network Analysis with Triangular Fuzzy Ties
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Annamaria", "Porreca", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           email = "annamaria.porreca@uniroma5.it"),
    person("Fabrizio", "Maturo", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "fabrizio.maturo@unimercatorum.it"))
Description: Tools for directed social networks whose ties are triangular
    fuzzy numbers. The package implements the fuzzy centrality indices of
    Porreca, Maturo and Ventre (2025) <doi:10.1016/j.ijar.2024.109319>
    (fuzzy triangular ordered weighted averages, best paths and fuzzy degree,
    closeness and betweenness), with a choice of the method used to rank
    fuzzy numbers, and the exact computation of the alpha-cuts of every
    centrality index that is continuous and non-decreasing in the tie
    weights, obtained from two crisp evaluations per level by the extension
    principle, as described in Porreca and Maturo (2026, manuscript submitted for
    publication). Actors are compared through possibility and necessity
    degrees, with suprema located by interpolation or bisection on the
    levels, certified orderings, rank intervals and the fuzzy set of the most
    central actor. Simulators of fuzzy networks and of mouse-tracking
    questionnaire ratings, importers of questionnaire data, Monte Carlo
    approximations and a reproducible simulation study are included.
